ti-channel video programming distributors, and other digital platforms. The Television segment produces, acquires, markets, and distributes programming through the FOX broadcast network; advertising-supported video-on-demand service Tubi; and operates full power broadcast television stations, including duopolies and other digital platforms. This segment also produces content for third parties. It also engages in the consumer finance marketplace; and provision of television and film production services along with office space, studio operation services, and all operations of the facility. Fox Corporation was incorporated in 2018 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Lachlan Keith Murdoch | Executive Chairman & CEO | Age 54 | Compensation: $16.5M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 10K people. Revenue per employee of $1.6M ranks in the top quartile among Communication Services peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $139K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $13K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Fox Corporation is a large-cap communication services business with a $38.9B market cap on $17.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $1.5B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.17\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.7\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 5.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (24.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Advertising-cycle exposure and content/regulatory risk \u2014 a single platform policy shift or ad-spend contraction cascades through the P&L quickly.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cord-cutting acceleration and audience fragmentation \u2014 legacy distribution bundles unravel faster than subscription revenue can replace them.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 22% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Valued at a 28% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"FOX (NASDAQ:FOXA) Coverage Initiated by Analysts at Morgan Stanley","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/fox-nasdaqfoxa-coverage-initiated-by-analysts-at-morgan-stanley.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794575254.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Illinois Municipal Retirement Fund Buy